    <name>Apollo 11 Early Apollo Scientific Experiment Package</name>
    <type>Spacecraft</type>
    <naif_host_id>A11E</naif_host_id>
    <description>The Apollo 11 Early Apollo Scientific Experiment Package (EASEP) contained the first experiments deployed on the Moon and served as a precursor to the Apollo Lunar Surface Experiments Packages (ALSEP) that were deployed during future Apollo missions. EASEP experiments included a laser ranging retroreflector (LRRR), a passive seismic experiment (PSE), a solar wind composition (SWC) experiment, and a lunar dust detector.             </description>
